module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.DifferentialsRepresentable
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExtensionByZeroUnitULift
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.AffineObjectDifferentialFormsNaturality

/-!
# Divided power differentials of a sheaf of rings on a site

Let `𝒞` be a site, let `φ : 𝒜 ⟶ ℬ` be a map of sheaves of commutative rings on `𝒞`, let
`𝒥 ⊆ ℬ` be a sheaf of ideals and let `δ` be a divided power structure on `𝒥`.  A *divided power
`𝒜`-derivation* of `ℬ` into a sheaf `ℱ` of `ℬ`-modules is an `𝒜`-derivation `D` (it is additive,
satisfies the Leibniz rule and kills the sections coming from `𝒜`) obeying the divided power chain
rule `D (δ_n x) = δ_{n-1} x · D x` for every `n ≥ 1` and every local section `x` of `𝒥`.

This file constructs the *universal divided power `𝒜`-derivation*
```
d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} : ℬ ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}
```
and proves that it is the composite of the universal derivation `d_{ℬ/𝒜} : ℬ ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` of
[Stacks, Tag 04BL] with the quotient map `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` by the submodule generated by the
local sections `d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)`; these are the two assertions of
[Stacks, Tag 07IW].

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.PresheafDividedPowers` — divided powers on a presheaf of ideals of `ℬ`.
* `Crystalline.IsSiteDPDerivation` — the divided power chain rule for an `𝒜`-derivation.
* `Crystalline.siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf` — the presheaf of `ℬ`-modules `U ↦ Ω¹_{ℬ(U)/𝒜(U),δ}`
  of [Stacks, Tag 07HZ], with the restriction maps induced by those of `ℬ`.
* `Crystalline.siteDPDifferentials` — the sheaf `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`, the sheafification of that presheaf.
* `Crystalline.siteDPUniversalDerivation` — the universal divided power derivation `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`.
* `Crystalline.siteDPQuotient` — the map `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` from the sheaf of differentials
  of [Stacks, Tag 04BL].

## Main results

* `Crystalline.existsUnique_siteDPDesc` — every divided power `𝒜`-derivation of `ℬ` into a sheaf
  of `ℬ`-modules factors uniquely through `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`.
* `Crystalline.universalDerivation_postcomp_siteDPQuotient` — `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` is the composite of
  `d_{ℬ/𝒜}` with `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`.
* `Crystalline.siteDPQuotient_relation` and `Crystalline.existsUnique_siteDPQuotient_desc` — that
  map kills the local sections `d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)`, and every map out of
  `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` killing them factors uniquely through it: it is the quotient of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` by the
  submodule they generate.

## Implementation notes

The construction and its universal property, `Crystalline.existsUnique_siteDPDesc`, are stated
for an arbitrary site `C : Type u₁` with `Category.{v₁} C`, rings in `CommRingCat.{u}`, and
sheaves of modules with sections in the universe `max u w`, under the two instances that make
sheafification of presheaves of modules available there,
`HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}` and `J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}`.
This is the generality the crystalline site `Cris(X/S)` needs: its objects form a
`Type (u + 1)`, so its sheaves of modules are taken with sections in `Type (u + 1)`.  The
ring-level modules `Ω¹_{ℬ(U)/𝒜(U),δ}` live in the universe `u`, so the presheaf
`Crystalline.siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf` is their universe lift
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheafULift`).  The base `𝒜` is a presheaf of commutative rings with a
map `φ : 𝒜 ⟶ ℬ`, so that the inverse image `f⁻¹𝒪'` of the relative version may be used in its
presheaf form, and the divided powers are `Crystalline.PresheafDividedPowers`: divided powers on
an ideal of every ring of sections, compatible with every restriction map; a divided power
structure on a sheaf of ideals in the sense of `Crystalline.DividedPowerStructure`
([Stacks, Tag 07I2]) gives one by `Crystalline.DividedPowerStructure.toPresheafDividedPowers`.

The comparison with the sheaf of differentials `Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials.moduleOfDifferentials`
of [Stacks, Tag 04BL] is made in the setting of that construction: a small site, rings and
modules in one universe, and `𝒜` a sheaf.  The quotient of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` by the submodule generated
by a family of local sections is expressed by its universal property: a map out of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}`
kills that submodule exactly when it kills each of the generating sections, so
`Crystalline.existsUnique_siteDPQuotient_desc` characterises `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` as that
quotient up to unique isomorphism.

The relative version for a morphism of ringed topoi `(f, f♯) : (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪) ⟶ (Sh(𝒞'), 𝒪')` of the
source is the case `𝒜 = f⁻¹𝒪'`, `φ = f♯` of the construction here.  Its application to the
structure morphism `(X/S)_cris ⟶ Sh(S_Zar)`, giving `Ω_{X/S}` and `d_{X/S}` on `Cris(X/S)`, is
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/SmallSite/CrystallineDividedPowerDifferentials.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04BL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04BL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07HZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07HZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07I2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07I2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite
open Stacks.Sheaves.Differentials

universe w v u₁ v₁ u

namespace Crystalline

/-! ### Divided powers on a presheaf of ideals -/

section DividedPowers

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C]

/-- Divided powers on a presheaf of ideals of a presheaf `B` of commutative rings: an ideal of
every ring of sections with divided powers on it, every restriction map of `B` being a
homomorphism of divided power rings. -/
structure PresheafDividedPowers (B : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}) where
  /-- The ideal of sections over `U`. -/
  ideal (U : Cᵒᵖ) : Ideal (B.obj U)
  /-- The divided powers on the ideal of sections over `U`. -/
  dividedPowers (U : Cᵒᵖ) : DividedPowers (ideal U)
  /-- The restriction maps are homomorphisms of divided power rings. -/
  naturality {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (i : U ⟶ V) :
    DividedPowers.IsDPMorphism (dividedPowers U) (dividedPowers V) (B.map i).hom

variable {J : GrothendieckTopology C} [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]

/-- A divided power structure on a sheaf of ideals, read on the rings of sections. -/
def DividedPowerStructure.toPresheafDividedPowers {B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}}
    {I : (SheafOfModules.unit (ringSheaf B)).Submodule} (δ : DividedPowerStructure B I) :
    PresheafDividedPowers B.obj where
  ideal := sectionIdeal B I
  dividedPowers := δ.dividedPowers
  naturality := δ.naturality

end DividedPowers

/-! ### Maps out of the universe lift of the divided power differentials -/

section RingLevel

variable {A B : CommRingCat.{u}} {J : Ideal B} {f : A ⟶ B} {hJ : DividedPowers J}

/-- A derivation, with values in a module in any universe, obeying the divided power chain rule
descends to the module of divided power differentials. -/
def dpDescLinear {M : ModuleCat.{v} B} (D : M.Derivation f)
    (hD : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : B), x ∈ J → D.d (hJ.dpow (n + 1) x) = hJ.dpow n x • D.d x) :
    dpDifferentials f hJ →ₗ[B] M :=
  letI := f.hom.toAlgebra
  letI := Module.compHom (M : Type v) f.hom
  letI : IsScalarTower A B M := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  (dividedPowerDifferentialRelations (A := A) hJ).liftQ
    (D : _root_.Derivation A B M).liftKaehlerDifferential (by
      refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
      rintro _ ⟨⟨x, n⟩, rfl⟩
      have hdA : ∀ b : B,
          (D : _root_.Derivation A B M).liftKaehlerDifferential
            (KaehlerDifferential.D A B b) = D.d b :=
        fun b ↦ (D : _root_.Derivation A B M).liftKaehlerDifferential_comp_D b
      change (D : _root_.Derivation A B M).liftKaehlerDifferential
        (dividedPowerDifferentialRelation hJ x n) = 0
      simp only [dividedPowerDifferentialRelation, map_sub, map_smul, hdA]
      rw [hD n x x.2, sub_self])

/-- The descended map sends `dpd hJ b` to `D.d b`. -/
theorem dpDescLinear_d {M : ModuleCat.{v} B} (D : M.Derivation f)
    (hD : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : B), x ∈ J → D.d (hJ.dpow (n + 1) x) = hJ.dpow n x • D.d x) (b : B) :
    dpDescLinear D hD (dpd hJ b) = D.d b :=
  let _ := f.hom.toAlgebra
  let _ := Module.compHom (M : Type v) f.hom
  let _ : IsScalarTower A B M := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl
  (D : _root_.Derivation A B M).liftKaehlerDifferential_comp_D b

/-- Two linear maps out of the universe lift of the divided power differentials agreeing on every
lifted universal differential are equal. -/
theorem uliftDpDifferentials_hom_ext {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M]
    {α β : ULift.{w} (dpDifferentials f hJ) →ₗ[B] M}
    (h : ∀ b : B, α (ULift.up (dpd hJ b)) = β (ULift.up (dpd hJ b))) : α = β := by
  let _ := f.hom.toAlgebra
  have e : α.comp ULift.moduleEquiv.symm.toLinearMap =
      β.comp ULift.moduleEquiv.symm.toLinearMap := by
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (dividedPowerDifferentials_span (A := A) hJ) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
    exact h b
  exact LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ congrArg (fun L : dpDifferentials f hJ →ₗ[B] M ↦ L x.down) e

/-- A derivation with values in a module in the universe `max u w` obeying the divided power chain
rule descends to the universe lift of the module of divided power differentials. -/
def dpDescULift {M : ModuleCat.{max u w} B} (D : M.Derivation f)
    (hD : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : B), x ∈ J → D.d (hJ.dpow (n + 1) x) = hJ.dpow n x • D.d x) :
    ModuleCat.of B (ULift.{w} (dpDifferentials f hJ)) ⟶ M :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom ((dpDescLinear D hD).comp ULift.moduleEquiv.toLinearMap)

/-- The descended map sends the lifted `dpd hJ b` to `D.d b`. -/
theorem dpDescULift_d {M : ModuleCat.{max u w} B} (D : M.Derivation f)
    (hD : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : B), x ∈ J → D.d (hJ.dpow (n + 1) x) = hJ.dpow n x • D.d x) (b : B) :
    dpDescULift D hD (ULift.up (dpd hJ b)) = D.d b :=
  dpDescLinear_d D hD b

/-- Two maps out of the universe lift of the divided power differentials agreeing on every lifted
universal differential are equal. -/
theorem uliftDpDifferentials_ext {M : ModuleCat.{max u w} B}
    {α β : ModuleCat.of B (ULift.{w} (dpDifferentials f hJ)) ⟶ M}
    (h : ∀ b : B, α (ULift.up (dpd hJ b)) = β (ULift.up (dpd hJ b))) : α = β :=
  ModuleCat.hom_ext (uliftDpDifferentials_hom_ext h)

end RingLevel

/-! ### Divided power derivations on a site -/

section General

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  {A : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u}} {B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : A ⟶ B.obj)
  (δ : PresheafDividedPowers B.obj)

/-- **The divided power chain rule** for an `𝒜`-derivation `D` of `ℬ` into a presheaf of
`ℬ`-modules: `D (δ_{n+1} x) = δ_n x · D x` for every section `x` of the divided power ideal. -/
def IsSiteDPDerivation {M : PresheafOfModules.{v} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M φ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (n : ℕ) (x : B.obj.obj U), x ∈ δ.ideal U →
    D.d ((δ.dividedPowers U).dpow (n + 1) x) = (δ.dividedPowers U).dpow n x • D.d x

/-- A divided power derivation followed by a map of presheaves of modules is a divided power
derivation. -/
theorem IsSiteDPDerivation.postcomp {M N : PresheafOfModules.{v} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    {D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M φ} (hD : IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ D) (g : M ⟶ N) :
    IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ (D.postcomp g) := fun U n x hx ↦
  (congrArg (g.app U).hom (hD U n x hx)).trans (map_smul (g.app U).hom _ _)

/-- Postcomposing a derivation with two maps is postcomposing it with their composite. -/
theorem derivation_postcomp_postcomp {M N P : PresheafOfModules.{v} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M φ) (g : M ⟶ N) (h : N ⟶ P) :
    (D.postcomp g).postcomp h = D.postcomp (g ≫ h) := by
  ext U x
  rfl

/-! ### The presheaf of divided power differentials -/

/-- The presheaf of divided power differentials `U ↦ Ω¹_{ℬ(U)/𝒜(U),δ}`, with sections in the
universe of the rings, and with the restriction maps induced by those of `ℬ`, which are
homomorphisms of divided power rings. -/
def siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase : PresheafOfModules.{u} (ringSheaf B).obj where
  obj U := dpDifferentials (φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U)
  map {U V} i := dpMap (φ.naturality i) (δ.dividedPowers U) (δ.dividedPowers V)
    (δ.naturality i)
  map_id U := by
    refine dpDifferentials_ext fun b ↦ ?_
    have hb : B.obj.map (𝟙 U) b = b := by rw [B.obj.map_id]; rfl
    rw [dpMap_d (φ.naturality (𝟙 U)) (δ.dividedPowers U) (δ.dividedPowers U)
      (δ.naturality (𝟙 U)) b, hb]
    rfl
  map_comp {U V W} i j := by
    refine dpDifferentials_ext fun b ↦ ?_
    have hb : B.obj.map (i ≫ j) b = B.obj.map j (B.obj.map i b) := by
      rw [B.obj.map_comp]; rfl
    have e1 := dpMap_d (φ.naturality (i ≫ j)) (δ.dividedPowers U) (δ.dividedPowers W)
      (δ.naturality (i ≫ j)) b
    have e2 := dpMap_d (φ.naturality i) (δ.dividedPowers U) (δ.dividedPowers V)
      (δ.naturality i) b
    have e3 := dpMap_d (φ.naturality j) (δ.dividedPowers V) (δ.dividedPowers W)
      (δ.naturality j) (B.obj.map i b)
    exact e1.trans ((congrArg (fun x ↦ dpd (f := φ.app W) (δ.dividedPowers W) x) hb).trans
      (e3.symm.trans (congrArg (ConcreteCategory.hom
        (dpMap (φ.naturality j) (δ.dividedPowers V) (δ.dividedPowers W)
          (δ.naturality j))) e2).symm))

/-- The restriction maps of the presheaf of divided power differentials send `d b` to the
differential of the restriction of `b`. -/
theorem siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase_map_d {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (i : U ⟶ V) (b : B.obj.obj U) :
    (siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase φ δ).map i (dpd (f := φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b) =
      dpd (f := φ.app V) (δ.dividedPowers V) (B.obj.map i b) :=
  dpMap_d (φ.naturality i) (δ.dividedPowers U) (δ.dividedPowers V) (δ.naturality i) b

/-- **The presheaf of divided power differentials** `U ↦ Ω¹_{ℬ(U)/𝒜(U),δ}`, with its sections
lifted to the universe `max u w` of the modules over which the universal property is stated. -/
def siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf : PresheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B).obj :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheafULift (ringSheaf B).obj).obj
    (siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase φ δ)

/-- The universal divided power derivation into the presheaf of divided power differentials. -/
def siteDPPresheafDerivation :
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ) φ :=
  PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation'.mk
    (fun U ↦ ModuleCat.Derivation.mk
      (fun b ↦ ULift.up (dpd (f := φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b))
      (fun b b' ↦ congrArg ULift.up (dpd_add (φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b b'))
      (fun b b' ↦ congrArg ULift.up (dpd_mul (φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b b'))
      (fun a ↦ congrArg ULift.up (dpd_map (φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) a)))
    (fun _ _ i b ↦ congrArg ULift.up (siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase_map_d φ δ i b).symm)

/-- On sections the universal derivation into the presheaf is the lifted ring-level universal
divided power differential. -/
theorem siteDPPresheafDerivation_d (U : Cᵒᵖ) (b : B.obj.obj U) :
    (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).d b =
      ULift.up (dpd (f := φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b) := rfl

/-- The universal derivation into the presheaf obeys the divided power chain rule. -/
theorem isSiteDPDerivation_siteDPPresheafDerivation :
    IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ) := fun U n x hx ↦
  congrArg ULift.up (dpd_dpow (φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) n x hx)

/-- **The factorization of a divided power derivation through the presheaf of divided power
differentials.** -/
def siteDPPresheafDesc {M : PresheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M φ) (hD : IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ D) :
    siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ ⟶ M where
  app U := dpDescULift (D.app U) (hD U)
  naturality {U V} i := by
    refine uliftDpDifferentials_ext fun b ↦ ?_
    change dpDescULift (D.app V) (hD V)
        (ULift.up ((siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase φ δ).map i
          (dpd (f := φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b))) =
      M.map i (dpDescULift (D.app U) (hD U) (ULift.up (dpd (f := φ.app U) (δ.dividedPowers U) b)))
    exact (congrArg (fun z ↦ dpDescULift (D.app V) (hD V) (ULift.up z))
      (siteDPDifferentialsPresheafBase_map_d φ δ i b)).trans
      ((dpDescULift_d (D.app V) (hD V) (B.obj.map i b)).trans ((D.d_map i b).trans
        (congrArg (fun z ↦ M.map i z) (dpDescULift_d (D.app U) (hD U) b).symm)))

/-- The factorization through the presheaf recovers the derivation. -/
theorem siteDPPresheafDerivation_postcomp_desc
    {M : PresheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M φ) (hD : IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ D) :
    (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp (siteDPPresheafDesc.{w} φ δ D hD) = D := by
  ext U b
  exact dpDescULift_d (D.app U) (hD U) b

/-- Two maps out of the presheaf of divided power differentials agreeing after postcomposition
with the universal derivation are equal. -/
theorem siteDPPresheaf_hom_ext {M : PresheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B).obj}
    {α β : siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ ⟶ M}
    (h : (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp α =
      (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp β) :
    α = β :=
  PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun U ↦ uliftDpDifferentials_ext fun b ↦
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation.congr_d h (X := U) b

/-! ### The sheaf of divided power differentials -/

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u w}]

/-- **The sheaf of divided power differentials** `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`: the sheaf of `ℬ`-modules associated
with the presheaf `U ↦ Ω¹_{ℬ(U)/𝒜(U),δ}`, with sections in the universe `max u w`. -/
def siteDPDifferentials : SheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B) :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafification (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj)).obj
    (siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ)

/-- **The universal divided power `𝒜`-derivation** `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} : ℬ ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`: the sectionwise
universal divided power differential followed by the unit of sheafification. -/
def siteDPUniversalDerivation :
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (siteDPDifferentials.{w} φ δ).val φ :=
  (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction (J := J) (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj)).unit.app
      (siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ))

/-- The universal divided power derivation obeys the divided power chain rule. -/
theorem isSiteDPDerivation_siteDPUniversalDerivation :
    IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ (siteDPUniversalDerivation.{w} φ δ) :=
  (isSiteDPDerivation_siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp φ δ _

/-- The bijection between maps out of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` into a sheaf of modules and maps out of the
presheaf it is associated with. -/
abbrev siteDPHomEquiv (F : SheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B)) :
    (siteDPDifferentials.{w} φ δ ⟶ F) ≃ (siteDPDifferentialsPresheaf.{w} φ δ ⟶ F.val) :=
  PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj)

/-- Postcomposing the universal divided power derivation with a map of sheaves is postcomposing
the presheaf derivation with the corresponding map of presheaves. -/
theorem siteDPUniversalDerivation_postcomp (F : SheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B))
    (f : siteDPDifferentials.{w} φ δ ⟶ F) :
    (siteDPUniversalDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp f.val =
      (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp (siteDPHomEquiv φ δ F f) := by
  ext U x
  rfl

/-- **The universal property of `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`** ([Stacks, Tag 07IW]).  Every divided power
`𝒜`-derivation of `ℬ` into a sheaf of `ℬ`-modules factors through the universal divided power
derivation by a unique map of sheaves of modules.  The site and the base `𝒜` are arbitrary: `𝒜`
is a presheaf of commutative rings, so that `𝒜 = f⁻¹𝒪'` for a morphism of ringed topoi may be
used in its presheaf form, and the modules live in any universe `max u w` in which the site
admits sheafification. -/
@[stacks 07IW "the universal divided power 𝒜-derivation d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} : ℬ → Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} on a site"]
theorem existsUnique_siteDPDesc (F : SheafOfModules.{max u w} (ringSheaf B))
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' F.val φ) (hD : IsSiteDPDerivation φ δ D) :
    ∃! f : siteDPDifferentials.{w} φ δ ⟶ F,
      (siteDPUniversalDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp f.val = D := by
  refine ⟨(siteDPHomEquiv φ δ F).symm (siteDPPresheafDesc.{w} φ δ D hD),
    (siteDPUniversalDerivation_postcomp φ δ F _).trans
      ((congrArg (fun ψ ↦ (siteDPPresheafDerivation.{w} φ δ).postcomp ψ)
        ((siteDPHomEquiv φ δ F).apply_symm_apply _)).trans
        (siteDPPresheafDerivation_postcomp_desc.{w} φ δ D hD)), fun g hg ↦ ?_⟩
  exact (Equiv.eq_symm_apply _).mpr (siteDPPresheaf_hom_ext.{w} φ δ
    ((siteDPUniversalDerivation_postcomp φ δ F g).symm.trans
      (hg.trans (siteDPPresheafDerivation_postcomp_desc.{w} φ δ D hD).symm)))

end General

/-! ### Comparison with the sheaf of differentials -/

section Comparison

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  {A B : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : A ⟶ B)
  {I : (SheafOfModules.unit (ringSheaf B)).Submodule} (δ : DividedPowerStructure B I)

/-- **The map `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`** from the sheaf of differentials of [Stacks, Tag 04BL]: the
map through which `d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`, an `𝒜`-derivation, factors. -/
def siteDPQuotient :
    moduleOfDifferentials A B φ ⟶ siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj)).symm
    ((presheafDifferentialsEquiv φ.hom
      (siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers).val).symm
      (siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers))

/-- **`d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` is the composite `ℬ ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`** of the universal derivation
of [Stacks, Tag 04BL] with `Crystalline.siteDPQuotient`. -/
@[stacks 07IW "d_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} is the composite of d_{ℬ/𝒜} : ℬ → Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} with Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} → Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}"]
theorem universalDerivation_postcomp_siteDPQuotient :
    (universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp (siteDPQuotient φ δ).val =
      siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers := by
  have key : (universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp (siteDPQuotient φ δ).val =
      presheafDifferentialsEquiv φ.hom
        (siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers).val
        (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj) (siteDPQuotient φ δ)) := by
    ext U x
    rfl
  exact key.trans ((congrArg (presheafDifferentialsEquiv φ.hom
      (siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers).val)
    ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv (𝟙 (ringSheaf B).obj)).apply_symm_apply _)).trans
      ((presheafDifferentialsEquiv φ.hom
        (siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers).val).apply_symm_apply _))

/-- The local section `d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_{n+1} x) - δ_n(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)` of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}`, for a section `x`
of the divided power ideal. -/
def siteDPRelation (U : Cᵒᵖ) (n : ℕ) (x : B.obj.obj U) :
    (moduleOfDifferentials A B φ).val.obj U :=
  (universalDerivation A B φ).d ((δ.dividedPowers U).dpow (n + 1) x) -
    (δ.dividedPowers U).dpow n x • (universalDerivation A B φ).d x

/-- A map out of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` kills every `d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_{n+1} x) - δ_n(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)` exactly when
its composite with `d_{ℬ/𝒜}` obeys the divided power chain rule. -/
theorem kills_siteDPRelation_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringSheaf B))
    (g : moduleOfDifferentials A B φ ⟶ F) :
    (∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (n : ℕ) (x : B.obj.obj U), x ∈ sectionIdeal B I U →
      (g.val.app U).hom (siteDPRelation φ δ U n x) = 0) ↔
      IsSiteDPDerivation φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers
        ((universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp g.val) := by
  refine forall_congr' fun U ↦ forall_congr' fun n ↦ forall_congr' fun x ↦
    imp_congr_right fun _ ↦ ?_
  have e : (g.val.app U).hom (siteDPRelation φ δ U n x) =
      ((universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp g.val).d ((δ.dividedPowers U).dpow (n + 1) x) -
        (δ.dividedPowers U).dpow n x • ((universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp g.val).d x :=
    ((g.val.app U).hom.map_sub _ _).trans
      (congrArg (fun z ↦ (g.val.app U).hom
        ((universalDerivation A B φ).d ((δ.dividedPowers U).dpow (n + 1) x)) - z)
        ((g.val.app U).hom.map_smul _ _))
  exact e ▸ sub_eq_zero

/-- **The map `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` kills the local sections
`d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)`.** -/
@[stacks 07IW "Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} → Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} kills the sections d(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d(x)"]
theorem siteDPQuotient_relation (U : Cᵒᵖ) (n : ℕ) (x : B.obj.obj U)
    (hx : x ∈ sectionIdeal B I U) :
    ((siteDPQuotient φ δ).val.app U).hom (siteDPRelation φ δ U n x) = 0 :=
  (kills_siteDPRelation_iff φ δ _ (siteDPQuotient φ δ)).mpr
    ((universalDerivation_postcomp_siteDPQuotient φ δ).symm ▸
      isSiteDPDerivation_siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers) U n x hx

/-- **`Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}` is the quotient of `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` by the submodule generated by the local sections
`d_{ℬ/𝒜}(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d_{ℬ/𝒜}(x)`.**  Every map of sheaves of `ℬ`-modules out of
`Ω_{ℬ/𝒜}` killing those sections factors uniquely through `Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} ⟶ Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ}`. -/
@[stacks 07IW "Ω_{ℬ/𝒜} → Ω_{ℬ/𝒜,δ} is the quotient by the submodule generated by the sections
  d(δ_n x) - δ_{n-1}(x) d(x)"]
theorem existsUnique_siteDPQuotient_desc (F : SheafOfModules.{u} (ringSheaf B))
    (g : moduleOfDifferentials A B φ ⟶ F)
    (hg : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (n : ℕ) (x : B.obj.obj U), x ∈ sectionIdeal B I U →
      (g.val.app U).hom (siteDPRelation φ δ U n x) = 0) :
    ∃! h : siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers ⟶ F,
      siteDPQuotient φ δ ≫ h = g := by
  have hD := (kills_siteDPRelation_iff φ δ F g).mp hg
  obtain ⟨h, hh, huniq⟩ := existsUnique_siteDPDesc.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers F _ hD
  have comp : ∀ h' : siteDPDifferentials.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers ⟶ F,
      (universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp (siteDPQuotient φ δ ≫ h').val =
        (siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u} φ.hom δ.toPresheafDividedPowers).postcomp h'.val :=
    fun h' ↦ (derivation_postcomp_postcomp φ.hom _ _ _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun E ↦ E.postcomp h'.val) (universalDerivation_postcomp_siteDPQuotient φ δ))
  refine ⟨h, ?_, fun h' hh' ↦ huniq h' ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨_, _, u⟩ := universalDerivation_isUniversal A B φ F
      ((universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp g.val)
    exact (u _ ((comp h).trans hh)).trans (u g rfl).symm
  · exact (comp h').symm.trans
      (congrArg (fun k ↦ (universalDerivation A B φ).postcomp k.val) hh')

end Comparison

end Crystalline
